Body:
The end goal is to have Opencode use GPT 5.4 Medium by reading the setting from Opencode.json (not manually switching it to medium via the UI)

Following this example https://opencode.ai/docs/models/#custom-variants I attempted to create a "Thinking" variant (just following the example. If it worked I would then create a "Medium" variant)

That example creates the variant, but how do I set Build mode to use that variant? The docs don't appear to say how

I tried both of these (just attempting to mimic the json hierarchy hoping it would work), but they resulted in errors:

```
"build": { "model": "github-copilot/gpt-5/thinking" }
```

and
```
"build": { "model": "github-copilot/gpt-5", "variant": "thinking" }
```

My current Full opencode.json, using variants as suggested, which still shows in the UI as Build using GPT 5.4 High

```
{
    "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
    "provider": {
        "copilot": {
            "models": {
                "gpt-5.4": {
                    "variants": {
                        "plan-high": {
                            "reasoningEffort": "high",
                            "textVerbosity": "low"
                        },
                        "build-medium": {
                            "reasoningEffort": "medium",
                            "textVerbosity": "low"
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    },
    "model": "github-copilot/gpt-5.4",
    "agent": {
        "plan": {
            "model": "github-copilot/gpt-5.4",
            "variant": "plan-high"
        },
        "build": {
            "model": "github-copilot/gpt-5.4",
            "variant": "build-medium"
        }
    }
}
```

same error on most recent version as of posting this with no custom model config afaik, running on void linux:
